cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tessera or cite its specifications, please cite this repository as below."
title: "Tessera: spec-first polyglot reference implementations for TesseraID, TesseraHash, and TesseraSeal"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Samani
    given-names: Bahram
repository-code: "https://github.com/barum/tessera"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-06-08"
abstract: >-
  Tessera is a specification-first monorepo housing three post-quantum-era wire formats with
  byte-identical reference implementations in eight languages: TesseraID (a 41-byte sortable
  identifier with Standard and Hybrid-Logical-Clock variants), TesseraHash (a 73-byte SHAKE-256
  content hash), and TesseraSeal (an ML-KEM-1024 + AES-256-GCM encryption envelope with a
  key-committing UtC tag). Each project ships a normative whitepaper, a canonical Python
  reference, a canonical C ABI, and a cross-language known-answer-test conformance harness.
references:
  - type: report
    title: "TesseraID Whitepaper"
    authors:
      - family-names: Samani
        given-names: Bahram
    url: "https://github.com/barum/tessera/blob/main/TesseraID_Whitepaper.pdf"
  - type: report
    title: "TesseraHash Whitepaper"
    authors:
      - family-names: Samani
        given-names: Bahram
    url: "https://github.com/barum/tessera/blob/main/tessera-hash/latex"
  - type: report
    title: "TesseraSeal Whitepaper"
    authors:
      - family-names: Samani
        given-names: Bahram
    url: "https://github.com/barum/tessera/blob/main/tessera-seal/latex"
